      "body": "## Summary\n\nPrecompiled block-scaled DistMoE graphs can reference custom operators before the first eager routed-experts call that normally registers them.\n\nWhen the resolved DistMoE context uses block scaling, register those operators before constructing the context so artifact loading does not depend on an earlier eager invocation.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `pytest -q torchtitan/experiments/graph_trainer/tests/test_dist_moe.py` (20 passed)\n- Imported `dist_moe._blockscaled` and verified the operator namespace is registered.\n- Targeted pre-commit hooks passed except repository-wide Pyrefly failures in unrelated environment APIs.\n\n## Stack\n\nDraft stacked on #5211.\n",
